// Reset a just-reclaimed span's scavenge grace state to ACTIVE and, if the
// scavenger actually handed its pages back to the OS (DECOMMITTED), re-back and
// re-zero them and rebuild the intrusive free list before the owning P allocates
// from it — the free-list head/links lived in the discarded data pages. A span
// merely in its grace period (SEEN_FREE) still has an intact free list, so it just
// gets the reset. Caller holds __slab_lock, so this cannot race a concurrent
// scavenge of the same span.
function __slab_reback_span(span MachineWord)
